From 6bd4b97b00f670abe854cca5f56705799e87ad62 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 03:42:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: hub final gate reads the sampler's fresh
 sample instead of measuring again under the lock

Hub 2026-11-12 23:21 -> 2026-11-13 03:14Z (16 "Hub admission refused Kanban claim" lines in agent.log): top-priority
card t_01a19400313cfbda was claimed by the hub, then released 5 s later (unused_grant) with
dispatch_skipped claim_deferred detail=hub_cpu_unknown, about every 5 min, while
machine_metrics.read_hub_cpu_sample() was 0.5-4.5 s old at 23-32 % busy.

Five whys
Problem: the hub takes a Board lease for t_01a19400313cfbda and refuses it as hub_cpu_unknown under a fresh sample.
Why 1: the refusal comes from _final_hub_gate (the locked gate after the lease), not the pre-lease advisory --
  evidence: the advisory admitted (the claim/lease happened); the release carries unused_grant; the refusal log is
  hermes_cli.kanban_admission. The docstring's "pre-check before a Board lease" exists and passed.
Why 2: the locked gate never read the sampler's sample: it took its own ~1 s /proc/stat sample and counted the host
  twice around it, inside a 2.25 s hold budget, and every exit it could not finish in time returned hub_cpu_unknown
  (`_over_budget(started, cpu.WINDOW_S)` before sampling, `_over_budget(started)` after) -- evidence: base
  kanban_admission.py _final_hub_gate.
Why 3: in the hub gateway process the pre-sample work alone exceeds the 1.25 s left for it -- evidence: hub probes
  with the live config (root_limit on/50 %, cap 7, 9 boards): quiet process admits in 1.13 s; with in-process CPU
  contention _cap_full took 4.5-63 s and root_limit/max_in_progress/census/candidate_pool 1.3-2.9 s each, and
  every call returned hub_cpu_unknown without ever sampling. The gateway is a single busy Python process (load ~6,
  tui-notif-poller and delegation threads competing for the GIL).
Why 4: the design treated "independent sample under the lock" as the safety property and charged it against the
  same hold that serializes chat turns, so the only budget-safe answer on a busy process was to refuse -- and it was
  labelled as an unknown CPU reading, so it looked like a sampler problem (the stale-advisory alert never fired
  because the advisory was fine).
Root (happened): the final gate re-measured CPU under the lock instead of reading the sample the sampler already
  publishes, so its cost scaled with the gateway's GIL contention, and the pre-lease advisory could not predict the
  locked outcome -> lease, refuse, release, repeat.
Root (not caught): tests faked cm.sample with an instant return and a fast census; no test ran the gate with a slow
  locked census, and an overrun shared the hub_cpu_unknown code, so logs could not tell "unknown CPU" from "slow gate".
Recurrence: kanban_dispatch_skip.py records a 2026-11-12 hub flap (claim_deferred alternating capacity /
  hub_cpu_at_or_above_limit); same family (locked gate disagreeing with the pre-lease view), different reason.

Countermeasures
- root: _final_hub_gate re-reads cache/hub-cpu-sample.json through one reader, sampler_sample(), shared with the
  pre-lease advisory (same triple, same validation: numeric fields, 1-2 s window, 0-100 %, not future, <= 15 s
  old). No /proc/stat sample and no sleep under admission.lock; one census, no recount (nothing waits between it
  and the commit). The claimed event records the sampler's exact triple.
- root: the pre-lease advisory now demands PRELEASE_HEADROOM_MS (5 s) more freshness (<= 10 s), so a sample it
  accepts is still fresh when the locked gate reads it after the Board round-trip: a stale sampler defers BEFORE
  the lease instead of churning a grant.
- detection: a hold overrun is now hub_admission_overrun (added to kanban_queue_reason.CODES), never
  hub_cpu_unknown.
- proof: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_hub_admission_sampler_read.py, 10 tests, all fail on the base (RED) and pass
  after; 17 admission/sampler/worker-admission files, 503 tests, pass. Existing tests that faked cm.sample now feed
  the locked read via a `locked()` helper; the real-/proc/stat lock-hold contract test is replaced by one asserting
  the locked read happens under the lock, takes no sample and records the sampler's triple.

Card: t_01a1d2e5c4899f40
